# Line endings.
#
# This repo is built inside Linux containers (Dockerfile) and on Linux CI runners, but it is also
# edited on Windows machines where core.autocrlf=true converts every text file to CRLF on checkout.
# A CRLF Dockerfile or shell script fails inside a container in confusing ways (a shebang becomes
# "/bin/sh^M: not found"), and Prettier's default endOfLine is "lf", so CRLF would also show up as
# lint noise. Storing and checking out LF everywhere removes that whole class of problem.
#
# The git index already holds LF for every tracked text file, so this rule changes nothing that is
# committed; it only stops Windows checkouts from rewriting files to CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything a Linux container executes or parses must be LF even if text detection ever guesses wrong.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
bun.lock text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch their bytes.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
